.TH PSVectorReduceSum 3 2023-12-09 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSVectorReduceSum\fR \- Compute the sum of all the elements of vector

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSFloat  
.br
\fBPSVectorReduceSum\fR(\fIPSFloat *a\fR, \fIuint64_t length\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compute the sum of all the elements of vector \fIa\fR having length defined by \fIlength\fR.
.br
The function can take advantage of the available accelerations (both hardwware and software). By default, accelerations set in \fIPSGlobalAcceleration\fR are used, if any. However, the used accelerations methods can be changed via the \fIacceleration\fR member of the optional argument \fIopts\fR.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The sum of all the elements in the vector \fIa\fR or zero if \fIa\fR is \fINULL\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
